---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const m = '/media/wing';
---

<Base
  title="Front wing in ground effect"
  description="A 2D RANS ride-height sweep of an inverted NACA 4412 in ANSYS Fluent: downforce rises 47% as the gap closes, then stalls. Where to set the wing, and why."
  sheet="3 of 3"
  dwg="MDR-003"
  image="/media/wing/cfd_vel020.webp"
>
  <header class="cs-head wrap">
    <div class="cs-head__top label">
      <a href="/#work">← All work</a>
      <span>Independent study · 2026</span>
    </div>
    <h1>Front wing in <em>ground effect</em></h1>
    <p class="cs-head__lede">
      An F1 front wing runs centimetres off the road, where ground effect can add downforce or suddenly take it away. I
      mapped how downforce, drag and the flow change with ride height for a single wing element, and turned that into a
      ride-height recommendation.
    </p>

    <dl class="spec">
      <div><dt class="label">Sweep</dt><dd>11 ride heights, 250 → 15 mm</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="label">Peak</dt><dd>+47% downforce at a 44 mm gap</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="label">Then</dt><dd>−16% downforce, 4.5× drag by 15 mm</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="label">Tools</dt><dd>ANSYS Fluent · 2D RANS, k-ω SST</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <figure class="cs-media">
      <img src={`${m}/cfd_vel020.webp`} alt="Velocity contours around the inverted wing at a 50 mm ride height, with fast flow in the gap under the wing." />
    </figure>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="chapter" style="border-top: 0;">
      <div class="chapter__side label"><b>A</b>Set-up</div>
      <div class="chapter__body">
        <h2 class="h2">Validate first, <em>then</em> sweep.</h2>
        <div class="pair">
          <div class="table-scroll">
            <table class="data">
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Wing</td><td class="num">NACA 4412, inverted, chord 250 mm, 4° incidence</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Flow</td><td class="num">50 m/s, Re = 8.6 × 10⁵, moving ground</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Model</td><td class="num">Steady RANS, k-ω SST, coupled, 2nd order</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Mesh</td><td class="num">107 000–148 000 cells, 25 prism layers</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Sweep</td><td class="num">h/c 1.0 → 0.06, 11 cases, residuals 1e-5</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <div class="table-scroll">
            <table class="data">
              <thead>
                <tr><th scope="col">Validation, h/c 1.0</th><th scope="col">CFD</th><th scope="col">Reference</th></tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Downforce C<sub>L</sub></td><td class="num">0.902</td><td class="num">0.875–0.915</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Drag C<sub>D</sub></td><td class="num">0.0152</td><td class="num">0.0135 (turbulent)</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Wall y+ on wing</td><td class="num">≤ 1.8</td><td class="num">≈ 1 for SST</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figure class="fig reveal">
          <img src={`${m}/cfd_mesh.webp`} alt="Close-up of the CFD mesh with boundary-layer cells wrapped around the wing and along the road." loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Mesh at h/c 0.20: quad boundary layer wrapped round the wing and along the road, fanned at the sharp trailing edge. Reference values from NeuralFoil at the same Reynolds number and incidence.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter__side label"><b>B</b>Result</div>
      <div class="chapter__body">
        <h2 class="h2">Downforce climbs, plateaus, then <em>falls.</em></h2>
        <figure class="fig reveal">
          <img src={`${m}/ground_effect_curve.webp`} alt="Two charts: downforce coefficient against ride height, peaking near h/c 0.175, and efficiency against ride height." loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Downforce rises 47% as the gap closes to 44 mm, plateaus, then falls 16% by 15 mm while drag climbs 4.5×.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="trio reveal">
          <figure class="fig">
            <img src={`${m}/cfd_vel100.webp`} alt="Velocity contours at 250 mm ride height." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>h/c 1.0 (250 mm): attached flow, thin wake. C<sub>L</sub> 0.902.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="fig">
            <img src={`${m}/cfd_vel020.webp`} alt="Velocity contours at 50 mm ride height." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>h/c 0.20 (50 mm): gap flow accelerates; a small separated zone forms at the tail. C<sub>L</sub> 1.319.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="fig">
            <img src={`${m}/cfd_vel006.webp`} alt="Velocity contours at 15 mm ride height with a large separated wake." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>h/c 0.06 (15 mm): gap air reaches 99 m/s, but the rear 43% of the underside separates. C<sub>L</sub> 1.113.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <div class="prose">
          <h3>Why it stalls</h3>
          <p>
            Closing the gap speeds up the air under the wing, which adds suction. But the air then has to slow back down
            before the trailing edge, and the tighter the gap, the harder that recovery. Below about 44 mm the separated
            zone grows faster than the gap suction, so downforce falls and drag climbs.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="table-scroll reveal">
          <table class="data">
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col">h/c</th><th scope="col">Separates at</th><th scope="col">C<sub>L</sub></th><th scope="col">C<sub>L</sub> / C<sub>D</sub></th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="num">1.00</td><td class="num">none</td><td class="num">0.902</td><td class="num">59.4</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="num">0.20</td><td class="num">82% chord</td><td class="num">1.319</td><td class="num">43.7</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="num">0.06</td><td class="num">57% chord</td><td class="num">1.113</td><td class="num">16.4</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter__side label"><b>C</b>Recommendation</div>
      <div class="chapter__body">
        <p class="pull">Set the wing at 50 mm, <em>not</em> at the peak.</p>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            At h/c 0.20 the wing makes 99.5% of maximum downforce with 11% better efficiency, and keeps 6 mm of margin
            before heave or braking pitch push it onto the falling side, where downforce drops as the car sinks. That
            loop is the same physics behind porpoising.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <a class="next" href="/work/cafe-racer/">
      <span class="label">Next project</span>
      <span>Café Racer Concept <span class="arrow">→</span></span>
    </a>
  </div>
</Base>
